6. Metacognition

This one is especially important.

A thought process can be templated too.

Template:

* observation
* interpretation
* uncertainty
* alternative hypothesis
* desired outcome
* test
* next move

Mad Lib:

I notice [observation]. My default interpretation is [interpretation]. Possible alternatives are [alternatives]. What I want is [goal]. The best discriminating test is [test]. Therefore the next move is [action].

That means you can use Mad Lib structures to scaffold:

* self-reflection
* decision-making
* emotional regulation
* problem-solving
* belief revision
* planning

So yes — metacognition itself can be structured through role slots and operator templates.

