Why this matters

This gives a unified way to think about abstraction:

Level 1: Fill a template

Basic Mad Lib use.

Level 2: Infer the hidden template

Take an existing artifact and reverse-engineer the slot structure.

Level 3: Compare templates

See when two domains share topology.

Level 4: Transfer templates

Port the structure into another domain.

Level 5: Compile stable templates into operators

Once a template works repeatedly, it becomes a reusable computational primitive.

That is basically Pantheon’s larger move.

