Even stronger version

The best version is dynamic Mad Libs, where the slots are not just filled once.

The fillers can change over time.

So:

* the same character can move from ally-slot to antagonist-slot
* the same number can shift meaning when context changes
* the same motif can change emotional value when repeated later
* the same concept can migrate frames as the discourse evolves

That makes the system temporal:

Template_t + Context_t \rightarrow Instantiation_t
Instantiation_t \rightarrow Template_{t+1}

So the structure is alive, not static.

